.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "veRin": [{"id": "veRin", "headword": "वेणिन्", "headword_slp1": "veRin", "fold": "veRin", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "वेणिन् m. ‘having a hood like braided hair’, N. of a serpent-demon, MBh.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "veRini": [{"id": "veRinI", "headword": "वेणिनी", "headword_slp1": "veRinI", "fold": "veRini", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "वेणिनी f. a woman with braided hair, L.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "veRigamulaka": [{"id": "veRIgamUlaka", "headword": "वेणीगमूलक", "headword_slp1": "veRIgamUlaka", "fold": "veRigamulaka", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "वेणी—ग-मूलक n. the root of Andropogon Muricatus, L.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "veRidata": [{"id": "veRIdatta", "headword": "वेणीदत्त", "headword_slp1": "veRIdatta", "fold": "veRidata", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "वेणी—दत्त m. (also with भट्ट, शर्मन् &c.) N. of various authors and other men, Cat.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "veRidana": [{"id": "veRIdAna", "headword": "वेणीदान", "headword_slp1": "veRIdAna", "fold": "veRidana", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "वेणी—दान n. a ceremony performed at Prayāga (cutting off a braid of hair and offering it to the Ganges with gifts to the priests), RTL. 375.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "veRidasa": [{"id": "veRIdAsa", "headword": "वेणीदास", "headword_slp1": "veRIdAsa", "fold": "veRidasa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "वेणी—दास m. N. of a man, Cat.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "veRiButa": [{"id": "veRIBUta", "headword": "वेणीभूत", "headword_slp1": "veRIBUta", "fold": "veRiButa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "वेणी—भूत mfn. (hair) forming a braid, BhP.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "veRimaDavabanDu": [{"id": "veRImADavabanDu", "headword":